 "version": 1,
 "about": "visibility, owner_email and access for a given identity. A private corpus refuses every capability to anyone who is not its owner, on its access list, or the platform's own engine. The last two manifests are one corpus as a hub holds it (private_whole) and as the hub gives it to a caller that holds the read token and names nobody (private_redacted: no owner_email, access or license_note, and no granted_by or statements in the licence). The redacted one fits the schema and is judged exactly as the whole one for the platform's engine and for nobody. It cannot be judged for a named person, whose name is not in it; the hub never sends it to one.",
